  <issue>
  Extend Rule L052 to handle all statements
I would expect that rule L052 would append a semi-colon to all statements missing one, but it looks like its current intent is not to do this.  Can we extend the rule?

## Expected Behaviour

The following code
```
CREATE FUNCTION dbo.funxn (
    @incoming varchar(50)
) RETURNS int
AS
BEGIN
    DECLARE @result int
    IF 1 = 1 SET @result = 1
    ELSE
        BEGIN
            SET @result = 0
        END

    RETURN @result
END;
```
Lints to
```
CREATE FUNCTION dbo.funxn (
    @incoming varchar(50)
) RETURNS int
AS
BEGIN
    DECLARE @result int;
    IF 1 = 1 SET @result = 1;
    ELSE
        BEGIN
            SET @result = 0;
        END

    RETURN @result;
END;
```

## Observed Behaviour

The code passes linting.

